          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Chris Horn",
          "email": "chorn@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-10-28 22:24:22.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-21057 lnet: read the discovery NID pair under lp_lock",
        "message": "LU-21057 lnet: read the discovery NID pair under lp_lock\n\nlnet_peer_send_push() drops lp_lock before it reads lp_disc_dst_nid\nand lp_disc_src_nid. A ping reply can arrive between the two reads.\nlnet_discovery_event_reply() then sets both NIDs from the reply.\n\nThe Push then gets the primary NID as destination and the source\nNID from the reply. These NIDs can be on different networks. LNet\nfinds no route between them, and the Push fails with -EHOSTUNREACH.\nDiscovery of the peer fails. For a gateway, LNet marks the routes\nthrough it down.\n\nCopy both NIDs and reset them under lp_lock. Use the copies for the\nPush.\n\nAdd CFS_FAIL_DISC_PUSH_DELAY to hold the Push before LNetPut().\nNew sanity-lnet test_246 uses it. A delayed REPLY and a Push from\nthe peer then put the REPLY inside the window.\n\n    sanity-lnet test_246 on 3 tcp VMs\n    without the fix: 10 of 10 fail (discovery -113)\n    with the fix:    20 of 20 pass\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: dce2f7d198 (\"LU-14660 lnet: Fix destination NID for discovery PUSH\")\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nChange-Id: Ia32491ededfed2e607cdbe9aa1c4f3a0692fcd24\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
